<p class="updated">Last updated 23 September 2026</p>

<p class="short">Miqdar runs entirely on your device. Your profile, food log, and weight data are
  stored on your iPhone and, if you use iCloud, synced through your own private iCloud account.
  There is no account to create, we have no server that receives your data, and we do not collect,
  sell, or share your information.</p>

<h2>What Miqdar stores, and where</h2>
<p>Your profile (body metrics, goals, targets), your food and weight entries, saved foods, and
  meal photos are stored on your device.</p>
<p>If iCloud is enabled, this data syncs across your devices through Apple’s CloudKit in your own
  private iCloud account. Only you can reach it — we cannot.</p>

<h2>Artificial intelligence</h2>
<p>Food logging, coaching, and meal plans are powered by Apple Intelligence, Apple’s on-device
  foundation models. When a request needs more capability and your device supports it, Miqdar may
  use Apple’s Private Cloud Compute, which processes the request without retaining your data and
  without exposing it to us. No food descriptions, photos, or profile data are ever sent to us or
  to any third-party AI service.</p>

<h2>Health data</h2>
<p>If you choose “Fill from Apple Health,” Miqdar reads your weight, height, date of birth, and
  biological sex only to set your starting targets. This is read with your permission, used on your
  device, and never uploaded or shared. Miqdar does not write to Apple Health on its own.</p>

<h2>Photos</h2>
<p>Meal and nutrition-label photos you capture are analyzed on your device and stored with the
  related entry. They are not uploaded to us.</p>

<h2>Analytics and tracking</h2>
<p>Miqdar contains no analytics, no advertising, and no third-party trackers. It does not track you
  across other apps or websites.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>Miqdar is a general-audience wellness app and is not directed at children under 13.</p>

<h2>Deleting your data</h2>
<p>Because your data lives on your device and in your iCloud, removing the app — and its iCloud data
  from Settings ▸ your name ▸ iCloud — removes it. There is no server-side copy for us to hold.</p>

<h2>Not medical advice</h2>
<p>Miqdar provides general wellness estimates. It is not a medical device and is not a substitute
  for professional advice.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:support@luna.bh">support@luna.bh</a></p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, we will update the date above and post the revised policy here.</p>
